#!/bin/sh
# pre-push: every wall the league has, under the one command, before a push
# leaves this machine. Wired by `npm run hooks`, the step the board in
# AGENTS.md names, which a contributor runs once per clone; nothing wires it
# at install time any more, because npm runs a dev install inside a clone it
# is packing whenever an install-lifecycle script exists, and that made an
# offline git install impossible (the-tag-installs-offline). A push that
# skips this hook is not done: the ci workflow runs the same command on the
# pull request. It runs on the working tree, whatever ref is being pushed,
# so a tag push runs the board too.
#
# KAAL_TEST_COMMAND exists so a test can prove the hook fails when its command
# fails; it is a recorded decision in architecture/gates-v1 with a reopen
# condition, and it is not for skipping the walls. The way past a red wall is
# a recorded waiver in waivers/, never --no-verify.
${KAAL_TEST_COMMAND:-npm test}
